  "claim": "A Numba CUDA tiled kernel on the GTX 1650 computes exact int8-to-int32 and int32-to-int32 matrix products. For 1024x1024 matrices, int8 inputs use a 6 MiB working set versus 12 MiB for float32, while the naive integer kernel is about nine times slower than cuBLAS float32. The result separates storage savings from throughput: integer GPU advantage requires an optimized kernel and wider safe accumulation.",
